  "note": "A twelve-bar minor blues in D minor. Play short, light strums and leave air between them. The hard spot is bars nine and ten, where Dm, C, Bb and A7 go by two to a bar: practise that walk down on its own. After the last verse the band switches to a shuffle on Dm7. The lead guitar is left out.",
